{
  "comment": "Each case sets one JSON pointer on the named valid fixture and must fail for EXACTLY ONE reason. `defect` names the single expected ProvenanceDefect variant, and the test asserts the returned list has length one and equals it — a validator that returns a pile of errors is not precision. `schemaInvalid` records whether the JSON Schema alone rejects the case, asserted in BOTH directions so the marker table cannot drift. A pointer whose parent exists but whose key does not is an insertion, which is how the misspelled-field case is expressed.",
